        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}3x-2y&=15\\\\5x-4y&=27\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3,\\ y=-3$.",
          "worked": "Double the first equation, then subtract the second.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}6x-4y&=30\\\\(6x-4y)-(5x-4y)&=30-27\\\\x&=3\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into the first equation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}9-2y&=15\\\\-2y&=6\\\\y&=-3\\end{align*}$$",
