        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3,\\ y=3$.",
          "worked": "Multiply the first equation by $2$ and the second by $3$, then subtract.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}8x+6y&=42\\\\9x+6y&=45\\\\(9x+6y)-(8x+6y)&=45-42\\\\x&=3\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into the second equation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}9+2y&=15\\\\2y&=6\\\\y&=3\\end{align*}$$",
